WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.125
Here's AWS's starting point.

2
00:00:02.125 --> 00:00:08.020
The Health API reference defines the event:
its service, its type code and category,

3
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.274
its region, its times, its status,

4
00:00:10.274 --> 00:00:14.088
and newer fields such as
actionability and personas.

5
00:00:14.088 --> 00:00:16.700
The command line's describe
events lists them.

6
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.515
A second operation returns each
event's latest description,

7
00:00:20.515 --> 00:00:24.712
one to ten events at a time, and a
third names the affected resources.

8
00:00:24.712 --> 00:00:27.137
The API needs a qualifying support plan,

9
00:00:27.137 --> 00:00:30.150
or it answers with a
subscription-required error.

10
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:36.033
And AWS's policy examples grant a wildcard
over the describe actions; AWS publishes

11
00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:41.640
no read-only managed policy for Health,
and the full-access one includes writes.
